    ``bfloat16``
       enable bfloat16 cooperative matrix support on GFX11-11.5
+   ``bc250_mesh_direct_prim``
+      enable bounded direct provoking-vertex transport of live generic Mesh
+      per-primitive outputs on truthful GFX10 GFX1013 only. Requires the existing
+      ``bc250_mesh`` opt-in for Mesh exposure; does not change advertised limits,
+      enable fast launch, or enable replay. This is a source-only research path,
+      not general Mesh support. The API stage remains Mesh and the user shader
+      executes once; additional physical vertices are export copies.
+
+      Only monolithic Mesh plus fragment pipelines with static first provoking,
+      Position/indices and 32-bit generic output fields are admitted. Task,
+      multiview, VRS, Mesh-query-enabled devices, special raster outputs, shader
+      objects, libraries and output spilling are unsupported. Queries must not
+      be active during these draws. Original corner and primitive order is kept,
+      including explicit vertex interpolation and line endpoint order.
+
+      Creation fails explicitly if the distinct-payload bound
+      ``min(corners * max_primitives, max_primitives + max_vertices - 1)`` exceeds
+      256, if physical PARAM allocation exceeds 32 slots or mixes provoking-only
+      values with interpolated/explicit inputs, or if logical outputs plus private
+      metadata require output spilling. Such a failure is not proof that the
+      shader is irreducible. Mesh pipeline caches are bypassed under the existing
+      BC250 source-validation policy; this option also bypasses the NIR cache and
+      participates in the graphics compilation key. Bounded two-triangle probes
+      with a shared provoking vertex, swapped connectivity, and LS128 cross-wave
+      output handoff passed on BC250. This does not validate the full domain,
+      additional interfaces or topologies; keep this option research-only.
    ``emulate_rt``
       forces ray-tracing to be emulated in software on GFX10_3+ and enables
       rt extensions with older hardware.
